{
  "id": "nested-checked-record-perl-ordinary-full-installed",
  "kind": "installed",
  "revision": "902e5a399b777c466844b3fc09add71742e149b2",
  "command": "LEAN_BRIDGE_PERL_TEST_GLIBC_FLOOR='2.36' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_PERL_TEST='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_PERL_CASES='ordinary-full' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_PERL_OUTPUT='build/vo1505-nested-record-perl-902e5a3/ordinary-full/records' LEAN_NUM_THREADS='1' OMP_NUM_THREADS='1' MAKEFLAGS='-j1' CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL='1' node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=tap '--test-name-pattern=^installed nested checked-record Perl packages reproduce and relocate for ordinary-full$' tests/helpers/nested-checked-record-perl-installed-tests.mjs",
  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce the complete CPAN component and runtime archives. Author sources are removed before offline installation on four pinned Perl ABIs in both prebuilt-only and build-xs modes; the unchanged caller runs before and after moving the complete installed tree, giving sixteen executions per selection. The full API checks direct and repeated parameters, Array, List, Option, Product, both Except branches, Holder.packet and the active Choice.packet.value field, including exact per-site constructors, normalization, complete rejected-input snapshots and recovery. Checked-record Perl acceptance covers the established top-level Interval, Sized 3 and Bounded 0 101 forms plus the tested acyclic Packet, Holder and Choice forms through Array, List, Option, Product and Except copied positions. Generic, recursive and inherited checked records, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete CPAN packages from two author roots, remove author sources, install offline in prebuilt-only and build-xs modes, and replay unchanged callers after relocating each installation. The runs cover threaded and unthreaded Perl 5.36.3 and 5.38.2 with Lean 4.32.2 on Linux x64/glibc 2.36, an explicit 2.36 package floor and 64-bit machine words. The archive retains exact records, generated XS and source closure; prepared CPAN archives and installed binaries retain authenticated identities without copied bytes. Hosted glibc 2.38 release-floor acceptance remains assigned to the dedicated workflow.",
